      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MISS DELIGHTFUL (8) seems to prefer a good track, and on such a surface she improved sharply to finish second at Coleraine 12 days ago. She drops 1.5kg, and her breeding suggests she will only be even better with more time. On top for us in this. TAAJWAR (6) ran on strongly from well off the pace here just over 2 weeks ago when finishing third, and with an extra 150m being ideal, she can figure in the finish again. FLAWS AND SINS (4) will find this easier than his first couple of starts, and he will relish getting out to 1550m from 1200m. A form reversal is on the cards. BLACK HEX (2) has been racing well from a run of bad draws, and he will have the pole position this time. Cam Rawiller sticks with him and so do we. MONSOON INDI (9) has been building her fitness, and will have top hoop Rochelle Milnes in the saddle for the first time, which is always a positive lead. Stick with her.",
